# includes:  1 feature commit. The platform lists fifteen valuation kinds and
#            could compute five of them; this closes the calculation half of
#            the gap for the specialty kinds. Six new pure engine modules in
#            engine-wrapper behind seven /engine/v1 endpoints, and a dedicated
#            report skeleton per specialty kind.
#
#            qsbs.py — IRC §1202 eligibility for the attestation letter.
#              Per-test breakdown rather than a single verdict (the letter
#              names every failed requirement), exclusion % fixed by the
#              acquisition date, per-issuer cap as max($10M less prior
#              exclusions, 10x basis). The holding-period test compares the
#              calendar anniversary, not days/365.25 — a span holding two leap
#              days makes exactly-five-years read as "more than five", and the
#              statute says more than.
#
#            intangibles.py — one module for PPA and IP because they are the
#              same four methods differently orchestrated: relief-from-royalty
#              (optional Gordon terminal), MEEM (attrition survival from year
#              1, aggregate contributory charge), with-and-without, cost less
#              multiplicatively-layered obsolescence. Income methods gross up
#              by the §197 TAB fixed point 1/(1 − t·A) at the same full-year
#              convention as the flows they scale. purchase_price_allocation
#              values each listed intangible and takes goodwill as the
#              residual; a negative residual reports as a bargain-purchase
#              gain (805-30-25-2), never negative goodwill.
#
#            impairment.py — the three standards kept distinct because their
#              rules differ where it costs money: 350-20 caps the loss at the
#              goodwill on the books, 350-30 has no screen and no cap, and
#              360-10 screens against UNdiscounted flows — so a group whose
#              fair value is below carrying but whose undiscounted flows cover
#              it is explicitly reported unimpaired, the outcome analysts most
#              often have to defend to an audit committee.
#
#            esop.py — the level-of-value chain made explicit (controlling →
#              marketable minority → nonmarketable minority), with DLOC and
#              control premium refused together: they are one fact stated from
#              opposite sides, and if they disagree the report would carry
#              whichever the code picked. Repurchase obligation projected as a
#              survival process (10%/yr does not exhaust in ten years), priced
#              by default at the per-share value the same run concluded.
#
#            smb.py — SDE normalization (owner add-backs, replacement wage for
#              the second owner), build-up capitalization of earnings, SDE and
#              rule-of-thumb revenue multiples, weighted like the 409A
#              approaches — including refusing a weight on a method the inputs
#              could not support rather than renormalizing it away.
#
#            emi_csop.py — UMV and AMV per share (minority discount hits both,
#              the restriction discount is what separates them), Schedule 5 /
#              Schedule 4 limits tested at the UMV this engagement concluded
#              rather than a caller-supplied figure. EMI £30M/250-FTE/£250k/
#              £3M; CSOP £60k and no discounted strike.
#
#            main.py — /engine/v1/{qsbs,intangible,ppa,impairment,esop,smb,
#              emi-csop}. The free-form inputs-dict endpoints map TypeError
#              from a wrong kwarg name to the same 422 the engine's own
#              validation gets, so a misspelled field never surfaces as a 500.
#
